      "text": "Let's denote the length of Mateen's backyard as \\( l \\) meters and the width as \\( w \\) meters.\n\nGiven that walking the length 25 times corresponds to 1000 meters, we can write the first equation as:\n\\( l \\times 25 = 1000 \\)\n\nAnd since walking the perimeter 10 times also corresponds to 1000 meters, we can write the second equation as:\n\\( 2l + 2w = 1000 \\)\n\nNow, let's solve these two equations simultaneously to find the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\).\n\nFirst, solve the first equation for \\( l \\):\n\\( l = \\frac{1000}{25} \\)\n\\( l = 40 \\, \\text{meters} \\)\n\nNow, substitute \\( l = 40 \\) into the second equation:\n\\( 2(40) + 2w = 1000 \\)\n\\( 80 + 2w = 1000 \\)\n\\( 2w = 1000 - 80 \\)\n\\( 2w = 920 \\)\n\\( w = \\frac{920}{2} \\)\n\\( w = 460 \\, \\text{meters} \\)\n\nNow that we have the dimensions of the backyard \\( l = 40 \\) meters and \\( w = 460 \\) meters, we can find the area \\( A \\) using the formula for the area of a rectangle:\n\\( A = l \\times w \\)\n\\( A = 40 \\times 460 \\)\n\\( A = 18,400 \\, \\text{square meters} \\)\n\nSo, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\( \\boxed{18,400} \\) square meters.",
