      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "1. **Determine the length of one side of the backyard:**\n   - Since walking the length 25 times completes a kilometer, the total distance covered is \\( 25 \\times \\text{Length} = 1000 \\) meters.\n   - Therefore, the length of Mateen's backyard is \\( \\text{Length} = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\) meters.\n\n2. **Determine the width of the backyard:**\n   - To find the width, consider the perimeter walking 10 times. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by the formula \\( P = 2 \\times (\\text{Length} + \\text{Width}) \\).\n   - Given that the perimeter is \\( 10 \\times \\text{Length} = 10 \\times 40 = 400 \\) meters.\n   - So, \\( 2 \\times (\\text{Length} + \\text{Width}) = 400 \\) meters.\n   - Substitute the length \\( \\text{Length} = 40 \\) meters into the equation: \\( 2 \\times (40 + \\text{Width}) = 400 \\).\n\n3. **Solve for the width:**\n   - First, divide both sides of the equation by 2: \\( 40 + \\text{Width} = \\frac{400}{2} = 200 \\).\n   - Then, isolate the width by subtracting 40 from both sides: \\( \\text{Width} = 200 - 40 = 160 \\) meters.\n\n4. **Calculate the area of the backyard:**\n   - The area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by \\( A = \\text{Length} \\times \\text{Width} \\).\n   - Substitute the values of length and width: \\( A = 40 \\times 160 \\).\n\n5. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   - \\( 40 \\times 160 = 6400 \\).\n\nConclusion:\nThe area of Mateen's rectangular backyard is \\( \\boxed{800} \\) square meters.",
