      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to find the length and width of the rectangle. Let's denote the length by \\( l \\) and the width by \\( w \\).\n\nFirst, we use the information given to set up the following equations:\n1. The length \\( l \\) is such that walking the length 25 times equals 1000 meters:\n   \\[\n   25l = 1000\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( l \\):\n   \\[\n   l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\n2. The perimeter \\( P \\) of the rectangle is such that walking the perimeter 10 times equals 1000 meters:\n   \\[\n   10P = 1000\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( P \\):\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{1000}{10} = 100 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n   The perimeter of a rectangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   P = 2l + 2w\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known value of \\( l \\):\n   \\[\n   100 = 2(40) + 2w\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   100 = 80 + 2w\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( w \\):\n   \\[\n   2w = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   w = 5 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\nNow that we have the dimensions of the backyard, we can calculate the area \\( A \\) as:\n\\[\nA = l \\times w = 40 \\times 5 = 200 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{200}\\) square meters.",
